ntimatroid polyhedra 81\n\nReferences\n\n[1] E. Algaba, J. M. Bilbao, R. van den Brink and A. Jimenez-Losada, Cooperative Games on\n\nAntimatroids, Discrete Math. 282 (2004), 1–15.\n\n[2] A. Bj¨\n\norner, L. Lov´\n\nasz and P. R. Shor, Chip-ﬁring games on graphs, European Journal of Com-\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeometry of poset antimatroids (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1571065313000322)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; We prove that every antimatroid of poly-dimension 2 is a poset antimatroid, and demonstrate both graph and geometric characterizations of such antimatroids.\n\n## Electronic Notes in Discrete Mathematics\n\nDate: 15 May 2013\n\nPages: 169-173\n\nVolume: Volume 40\n\n## Published by: Elsevier\n\n# Geometry of poset antimatroids\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel Yulia Kempner, Vadim E. Levit\n\nShow more\n\nCite\n\nAdd to Mendeley\n\nShare\n\n10.1016/j.endm.2013.05.031\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nAn antimatroid is an accessible set system closed under union. A poset antimatroid is a particular case of antimatroid, which is formed by the lower sets of a poset. Feasible sets in a poset antimatroid ordered by inclusion form a distributive lattice, and every distributive lattice can be formed in this way. We introduce the polydimension of an antimatroid as the minimum dimension d such that the antimatroid may be isometrically embedded into d-dimensional integer lattice {\\mathbb{Z}}^{d}. We prove that every antimatroid of poly-dimension 2 is a poset antimatroid, and demonstrate both graph and geometric characterizations of such antimatroids. Finally, a conjecture concerning poset antimatroids of arbitrary poly-dimension d is presented.\n\n## Keywords\n\nAntimatroid\n\n;\n\nposet antimatroid\n\n;\n\ndimension\n\n\nView full text--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFaculty of Natural Sc